Improvements to template editor:
- Do preview subdomains respond to etags?
- Make preview hot reload more efficient by only reloading when the tab is visible
  - the injected script in `app/blog/render/middleware.js` and `app/blog/views/template-error.html` does `new EventSource('/__blot/preview/reload').onmessage = function() { window.location.reload(); }` on every message, including background tabs / hidden template-editor iframes. the expensive part is the full render that `location.reload()` triggers, not the SSE connection (keep that open; 10s heartbeats are cheap)
  - follow the visibility pattern in `app/views/js/sync_status.js`: if `document.visibilityState === "hidden"`, set a pending flag; on `visibilitychange` to visible, reload once
  - debounce? no long debounce. the server already publishes once per completed sync that had changes (`app/sync/index.js` after the cacheID bump), so events are not per-keystroke. coalesce instead: one pending reload is enough if several events arrive while hidden or while a reload is already in flight. a short (100–300ms) debounce would only matter for back-to-back completed syncs while the tab is visible
  - etags? not nicely, not yet. `location.reload()` may send If-None-Match / If-Modified-Since and openresty already forwards those (`proxy/config/reverse-proxy-preview.conf`). render middleware sets Last-Modified from cacheID and Express default weak etags come from the body, but freshness is checked in `res.send()` after the expensive render, so a 304 still costs a full render. skipping the reload when hidden is the real win. a cheap cacheID-based etag checked *before* render would actually leverage them — related to the etag question above
- Add [commit mono](https://commitmono.com/) font to font picker
- File upload feature (_url) needs to generate image dimensions too.. maybe it needs MORE power
- Enforce size limits on setting tempalte views
